worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/yaw_aug_xrir_fable_code_branch_review.md:24:- **Why it matters.** During the merge the index holds staged changes under `tools/` and `tests/`, so `checked_git_state` reports `dirty_outside_worklog` and **any evaluation launched in that window is refused at setup** (the same failure as the three `_ABORTED_setup_failed` runs). The queue starts the next run within seconds of the previous `END`, so the merge must start right after a `START` line of a long run (a block run takes ≈ 50 min; `aug_k8_seed43_block` started 15:26:36) and finish — conflict resolved, committed — well inside it. Prepare the resolved notebook text beforehand.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/yaw_aug_xrir_fable_code_branch_review.md:27:- **Where.** Scratchpad `exp04_eval_queue.sh` (outside the repository): `run_eval aug_k8_seed42_grid simple $ck 8 42 "0 4 8 16 32 64 96 128 192 256 320 384 416 448 480 496 504 508" $B`, and `run_eval` passes the same `$cols` to both `--yaw-cols` and `--acoustic-cols`. Profile `tools/exp04_profiles.py:129-136`: `GRID_SEED42` has `grid = SPECTRAL_GRID` (18) and `acoustic_grid = ACOUSTIC_GRID = (0, 8, 32, 64, 128, 256, 384, 448, 480, 504)` (10). `tools/paired_compare.py:389-390` requires `acoustic_cols == acoustic_grid` exactly, and `:396-397` requires EDT/C50/T60 to be present **only** at acoustic-grid angles.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/yaw_aug_xrir_fable_code_branch_review.md:28:- **What.** The queued run computes acoustic metrics at all 18 angles (≈ 2 h of GPU instead of ≈ 1 h) and `tools/exp04_descriptive.py --profile GRID_SEED42` will refuse it (`grid acoustic_cols`, `metric coverage edt`). The round-8 close review flagged exactly this requirement ("`--acoustic-cols` = the 10 acoustic columns … the queue script lives outside the repository, so I could not verify its flags"); I could now verify it. The k = 0, block (`aug`: 8 angles = `BLOCKS['aug']`; `control`: 5 = `BLOCKS['control']`) and `aug9_k8_seed*_k0` lines are consistent with their profiles (`acoustic_grid` absent → `acoustic_cols == run grid`), and the aug `--bind-input` lines match A6. The producers resolve both checkpoint paths (`paired_compare.py:350`), so the `attempt_20260913T102051/…` paths in the live manifests are admitted through the `final` symlink.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_04_yaw_aug_xrir_claude/yaw_aug_xrir_fable_code_branch_review.md:29:- **Options (Planner's call; no signal to any process is needed).** (a) Before the queue reaches the grid line (after the four remaining block runs, ≈ 18:45), create an empty placeholder directory `ckpt/yaw_aug/eval/aug_k8_seed42_grid`; the queue's `[ -e "$out" ] && SKIP` then skips it; after the chain, remove the placeholder and launch the grid manually with `--yaw-cols "<18 spectral>" --acoustic-cols "0 8 32 64 128 256 384 448 480 504"` and the two `--bind-input` flags (the launcher creates the run directory exclusively, so the placeholder must be gone). Do **not** edit the running queue script in place (bash reads it incrementally). (b) Let the run happen and relaunch a corrected one afterwards under the same label after moving the wrong run aside (costs ≈ 2 h GPU). (c) Amend the profile to `acoustic_grid = SPECTRAL_GRID` — a Coder round on `tools/exp04_profiles.py`, which is in all four producer closures (digests change; must land before the A9 fill) and needs review; not recommended.
